          "label": "C",
          "text": "5",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "6",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "Shortcut: Integrate each term using power rule: ∫3x^2 dx = x^3, ∫2x dx = x^2, ∫1 dx = x. Evaluate from 0 to 1: (1^3+1^2+1) - 0 = 3. Full solution: The antiderivative is x^3 + x^2 + x. Substituting the limits gives 1+1+1 = 3.",
